I approach Clario as an **AI native marketing workflow**: the campaign context, evidence and review steps shape what the AI is asked to do. A request begins with a specific finding and a bounded set of measurements. The model proposes an explanation and a test against that context; it must refer to the supplied evidence and identify missing information.

Metric calculations and rule-based checks establish the factual starting point. Generated explanations add possibilities that still need judgment. If the AI service is unavailable, the manual hypothesis form remains usable. The product does not need to invent an answer to keep the marketer moving.
